      "rank": 1,
      "ticker": "NASDAQ:CHRS",
      "symbol": "CHRS",
      "date": "2026-10-28",
      "title": "Study result",
      "tag": "study / data update",
      "url": "https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/chrs/transcripts/771295-study-result/",
      "core": true,
      "briefed": true,
      "brief_file": "summary-chrs-study-result-oct28.md",
      "tldr": [
        "Coherus reported compelling interim tagmokitug data in esophageal squamous cell carcinoma (ESCC): first-line confirmed ORR was 75% at the October 14 cutoff and 89% after two post-cutoff scans, while PD-L1-positive ORR remained 100%; second-line data at the 700 mg dose showed a confirmed ORR of 16.7%, 33.3% clinical benefit rate, and 5.5-month median PFS.",
        "Management is prioritizing an integrated ESCC development plan: expand first-line cohorts to 30–40 patients, mature durability data, align on the 700 mg dose with the FDA in first-quarter 2027, and potentially pursue accelerated approval for first- and second-line indications.",
        "Activity was also observed in head-and-neck, upper-GI adenocarcinoma, and colorectal cancer, generally concentrated at 700 mg; management characterized safety as manageable, with no new safety signals or grade-five tagmokitug-related events."
      ],
      "on_watchlist": true
    },
    {
      "rank": 2,
      "ticker": "NYSE:COUR",
      "symbol": "COUR",
      "date": "2026-10-29",
      "title": "Earnings Call: Q3 2026",
      "tag": "earnings call",
      "url": "https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/cour/transcripts/718708-q3-2026/",
      "core": true,
      "briefed": true,
      "brief_file": "summary-cour-q3-2026-earnings.md",
      "tldr": [
        "Q3 revenue was $377M, up 94% as reported but down approximately 3% on a normalized basis; adjusted EBITDA was nearly $62M, with a 16.3% margin.",
        "Integration is ahead of schedule: management expects more than $150M of annualized gross cost savings by year-end and the $115M net run-rate synergy target within eight months of the May close.",
        "Growth remains the main weakness: normalized consumer revenue fell 9%, enterprise revenue grew 2%, and management’s directional 2027 baseline assumes roughly flat to modestly declining enterprise revenue and a low-double-digit consumer decline."
      ],
      "on_watchlist": true
    },
    {
      "rank": 3,
      "ticker": "NYSE:CCJ",
      "symbol": "CCJ",
      "date": "2026-10-30",
      "title": "Earnings Call: Q3 2026",
      "tag": "earnings call",
      "url": "https://stockanalysis.com/quote/tsx/CCO/transcripts/721310-q3-2026/",
      "core": true,
      "briefed": true,
      "brief_file": "summary-ccj-q3-2026-earnings.md",
      "tldr": [
        "Q3 and nine-month 2026 results declined year over year as expected, primarily due to the longer planned Key Lake mill outage, higher associated costs, and a prior-year Westinghouse payment related to the Korean Dukovany project.",
        "Cameco narrowed 2026 production and delivery guidance, but raised expected direct administrative and average unit costs; full-year CapEx was reduced because some mining and fuel-services work moved beyond 2026.",
        "Management remains bullish on nuclear fundamentals and U.S. new-build activity, but is maintaining production, contracting, and financial discipline while uranium contracting remains below replacement rate."
      ],
      "on_watchlist": true
    },
    {
      "rank": 4,
